 "purpose": "Sentence analysis (zinsontleding) as an exercise: the steps, checking, thinking errors, hints, explanations, free colouring, dividing into parts, the cheat sheet and the Onderwerp that makes the questions.",
 "details": "Step by step as at school (pv, then o, then lv, then mv; on harder levels also the predicate and the adverbial): a hint with the school question ('wie of wat + pv?'), a try with a second chance and an explanation. In each step the child chooses words (a tuple of positions) or says that the part does not exist (None). A sentence with more than one pv first asks all pv's (step 'pv') and then the subject of each pv (steps 'o1', 'o2', ...; soort('o2') is 'o' for name and colour). The Zinsontleding class (registered as ZINSONTLEDING at the bottom of the file) makes the questions from the leerlijn: sentences from the machine, the hand-checked list, or compound sentences, in proportions set by the leerlijn. The input object that plays the steps is terminal/zinsdelen.py. No curses.",
 "module_docstring": "Zinsontleding: de stappen, het nakijken, de denkfouten, de tips (de proefjes) en de uitleg. Zonder curses.",
